{"data":{"attachmentkeynames":["rs"],"desc":"The resource map (spectrum S1): per-GPU total/free memory and free disk where the model subsystem lives. Reads the service's /status resources block when the service answers (torch's view); falls back to nvidia-smi directly when it doesn't, so the map is never absent. Empty gpus on a CPU-only box is an answer, not an error; a GPU whose memory nvidia-smi reports [N/A] (unified-memory parts like GB10) is listed with unmeasurable:true instead of dropped. Disk is probed at the model dir or its first existing ancestor, so the disk fact survives the model subsystem being off. Customers: the posture solver, ring byte-budget warnings, birth-run sizing.","import":"use ndata::dataobject::DataObject;\nuse ndata::dataarray::DataArray;\nuse flowlang::datastore::DataStore;\nuse flowlang::flowlang::system::system_call::system_call;\n/// Windows: physical memory total and available, in MB (GlobalMemoryStatusEx).\n#[cfg(windows)]\npub fn win_memory_mb() -> Option<(i64, i64)> {\n  #[repr(C)]\n  struct MemoryStatusEx { length: u32, memory_load: u32, total_phys: u64, avail_phys: u64,\n    total_page: u64, avail_page: u64, total_virtual: u64, avail_virtual: u64, avail_extended: u64 }\n  #[link(name = \"kernel32\")]\n  extern \"system\" { fn GlobalMemoryStatusEx(b: *mut MemoryStatusEx) -> i32; }\n  let mut m: MemoryStatusEx = unsafe { std::mem::zeroed() };\n  m.length = std::mem::size_of::<MemoryStatusEx>() as u32;\n  if unsafe { GlobalMemoryStatusEx(&mut m) } == 0 { return None; }\n  Some(((m.total_phys / 1048576) as i64, (m.avail_phys / 1048576) as i64))\n}\n#[cfg(not(windows))]\npub fn win_memory_mb() -> Option<(i64, i64)> { None }\n\n/// Windows: bytes free to this user on the volume holding `p` (GetDiskFreeSpaceExW).\n#[cfg(windows)]\npub fn win_disk_free_bytes(p: &std::path::Path) -> Option<u64> {\n  use std::os::windows::ffi::OsStrExt;\n  #[link(name = \"kernel32\")]\n  extern \"system\" { fn GetDiskFreeSpaceExW(dir: *const u16, avail: *mut u64, total: *mut u64, free: *mut u64) -> i32; }\n  let w: Vec<u16> = p.as_os_str().encode_wide().chain(Some(0)).collect();\n  let (mut a, mut t, mut f) = (0u64, 0u64, 0u64);\n  if unsafe { GetDiskFreeSpaceExW(w.as_ptr(), &mut a, &mut t, &mut f) } == 0 { return None; }\n  Some(a)\n}\n#[cfg(not(windows))]\npub fn win_disk_free_bytes(_: &std::path::Path) -> Option<u64> { None }\n","params":[],"returntype":"JSONObject","type":"rust"},"id":"qzikks1a01776d049o1","readers":[],"time":1794894799369,"username":"system","writers":[]}